{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1199294-apocalypse-form-ideas","id":1199294,"title":"Apocalypse Form: Ideas!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-24T21:01:52-07:00","id":1199294,"title":"Apocalypse Form: Ideas!","content":"So, I've recently taken up an interest in Demon the Fallen, and decided to try writing up some ideas regarding apocalypse forms for use by either players or NPC's. Sadly, we don't have a Fallen related forum, so I decided to post this in the general section for World of Darkness. <br /> <br /> Of course, if any of you have your own ideas for apocalypse forms, feel free to chip in!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Lammasu Adad:</b> The skeleton, organs, blood vessels and nervous system of a humanoid figure as normal. But instead of flesh and skin, it is composed of salt water, who's rippling surface can mold its outward appearance as desired. The transparency of the saltwater is related to their level of Torment, with their internal structure becoming more visible the higher it rises. Obviously, seeing exposed nerves and organs can be quite shocking to those with weaker constitutions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rabisu Zaltu:</b> An anthropomorphic snapping tortoise who's body is protected by an armored shell. Its digits end in hooked claws, and its mouth is like a razor sharp beak. Its powerful muscles afford it tremendous strength in battle. At high levels of torment, the demon takes on a more decayed appearance. Blood seeping from between a cracked shell as scales peel away to expose patches of muscle tissue beneath the surface.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Namaru Qingu:</b> An impossibly beautiful man or woman who's naked form is censored by a dense aura of light radiating from the appropriate zones on their body. Their voice is both compassionate and authoritative, punctuated by a soft echo layered beneath it. At high levels of Torment, their aura becomes physically uncomfortable to look at and the compassion in their voice is replaced with spiteful contempt. The echo of their voice also becomes deeper pitched, instilling those who hear it with a sense of menacing danger.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Halaku Namtar:</b> An elderly man with ghost white skin and a gaunt frame wearing the funerary robes of a priest. His eyes are concealed behind reflective glasses and his voice speaks with a deadpan monotone. At high Torment, the man's form decays into a bleached skeleton as the robes become tattered rags and its voice becomes a rasping hiss. Without ears to hold them in place, the glasses fall away to reveal two pinpricks of red light shining from the demon's eye sockets.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I would have written one for the <b>Annunaki</b> (thus including one from each house), but they seem to be the hardest for me to think up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}